ean Star Offshore Drilling Rig Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":29.311414,"lo":-94.790642,"d":277,"ds":"The Ocean Star Offshore Drilling Rig & Museum, located in Galveston, Texas, is a museum dedicated to the offshore oil and gas industry. Located next to the Strand National Historic Landmark District, the museum is housed on a retired jack-up rig set up in the Galveston harbor.","wpu":"Ocean Star Offshore Drilling Rig & Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Ocean_Star_Offshore_Drilling_Rig_And_Museum.jpg/960px-Ocean_Star_Offshore_Drilling_Rig_And_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Galveston Railroad Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":29.306551,"lo":-94.796919,"d":539,"h":"Mo-Su 10:00-17:00","w":"https://galvestonrrmuseum.org/","ad":"123 Rosenberg Avenue - 25th Street","ds":"The Galveston Railroad Museum is a railroad museum housed in the former Santa Fe Railroad station, at 25th and Strand in Galveston, Texas. The Museum is owned and operated by the Center for Transportation and Commerce, a non-profit organization. The museum was established with funds from Galveston businesswoman and philanthropist Mary Moody Northen and the Moody Foundation.","wpu":"Galveston Railroad Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Old_Santa_Fe_Union_Station.jpg/960px-Old_Santa_Fe_Union_Station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Galveston Railroad Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":29.305992,"lo":-94.79806,"d":662,"h":"Mo-Su 10:00-17:00","w":"https://www.galvestonrrmuseum.org","ph":"+1 409 765 5700","ad":"2602 Santa Fe Place","ds":"The Galveston Railroad Museum is a railroad museum housed in the former Santa Fe Railroad station, at 25th and Strand in Galveston, Texas. The Museum is owned and operated by the Center for Transportation and Commerce, a non-profit organization. The museum was established with funds from 